SM(179,{"n":"1 Peter 4.12 - 5.14","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Peter 4.12 - 5.14.mp3","d":2129.6,"s":[[0.16,"Writing, and so we've seen he's taken sort of two approaches over the last couple of couple of chapters we've read."],[6.08,"First of all, to remind them of Christ's sufferings, how Christ suffered and died, was killed by sinful men and then entered into his glory."],[17.0,"And so if they share inside Christ's sufferings, they will also share in his glory."],[21.81,"So on that side to remind them of Christ's second coming, and then relatedly on the other side to say, because of this, within your community, within the Christian community, there needs to be love, there needs to be mutual support."],[38.23,"You need to be united there for each other, supporting each other."],[42.41,"Full of love for each other, doing good for each other in the face of what's coming at you from the outside world."],[49.21,"So solidarity for Christians as they prepare for Christ's second coming, and then reminder that when they face that suffering, uh, to make sure that that suffering is unjust, as he says."],[64.84,"Don't get persecuted for doing actual bad things, because then it's not persecution."],[69.85,"But if you're persecuted for doing good, then you know that you are like Christ, suffering for what is right."],[77.13,"And if you share in his suffering, you'll also share in his glory."],[80.25,"So that's sort of a real quick summary of sort of what St."],[83.45,"Peter has been talking about."],[85.29,"Um that's where we're gonna pick up here."],[87.45,"So, unless anybody has any leftover questions or comments or news reports, or today's lucky lotto numbers, we'll start uh here in St."],[99.69,"Peter's first epistle, chapter. four, verse twelve"],[104.29,"Beloved, do not think it strange concerning the fiery trial which is to try you, as though some strange thing happened to you, but rejoice to the extent that you partake of Christ's sufferings, that when his glory is revealed, you may also be glad with exceeding joy."],[121.59,"So he's picking up with again, reiterating exactly what we were just talking about."],[125.93,"Sort of summarizing what he said in the last chapter or two."],[130.59,"So when these things come upon you, these seven years go upon you, you said, don't act like this is some strange thing."],[136.75,"Meaning, don't say, Why?"],[138.99,"Why is this happening?"],[140.57,"What He says, just remember."],[142.91,"This is Christ suffered."],[143.47,"Christ was sinless, but he suffered at the hands of wicked people"],[150.21,"And that means if this happens to you too, that means you're like Christ."],[154.47,"And so when his glory is revealed, when he appears again, that you will also share in his glory and with joy."],[164.63,"Verse 14. Okay, so now he's talking about the Holy Spirit."],[176.63,"So the fact that you would be persecuted for Christ or mocked for following Christ or marginalized or shunned for following Christ."],[187.41,"This is a sign that the Holy Spirit is within you."],[191.74,"This is a sign."],[193.58,"Now, so this is this is going against the way not only people of the agent world, but the way we normally operate."],[201.95,"So if uh you or I made a major life decision, I'm gonna join this group, I'm gonna join this club, I'm gonna go try and get this degree, I'm gonna go, you know right, we're embarking on an endeavor."],[213.55,"And as soon as we embark on it, sort of everything seems to start going wrong."],[218.93,"Most of us would conclude, well, maybe I shouldn't be doing this."],[223.9,"Maybe I should just forget it."],[226.24,"It seems like all the signs are this is the wrong thing for me to do."],[228.8,"So this is what St"],[230.76,"And that was natural in the ancient world, too."],[235.96,"Peter is speaking to."],[237.09,"So this would have been a temptation."],[238.37,"You have these people who are members of the Jewish community in the synagogue."],[242.85,"They've decided now to follow the people who have come to them, the apostles, like St."],[248.29,"Peter, St. Paul, who have come to them preaching that Jesus of Nazareth is the Messiah."],[253.55,"Say, oh wow."],[254.69,"This sounds good."],[255.73,"This gospel thing, we're on board."],[257.91,"They decide to join the Christian part of that community, and now they're forced out of their homes in Rome."],[265.37,"They're shunned by society."],[267.06,"Everything is sort of falling apart."],[270.36,"And even within the Christian community itself, if St."],[273.24,"Peter is having to tell them they need to love one another and stuff, that means they're not all doing that right now."],[279.66,"So even within the Christian community, there's people they don't get along with."],[284.32,"There's problems, there's issues, there's difficulties."],[288.24,"So it would have been very easy for any of them to just say, why am I doing this again?"],[295.73,"Are you sure this is true?"],[297.33,"If this is true, why did everything goes bad as soon as I joined?"],[300.77,"Maybe I need to just go back to right where I was."],[306.09,"When things were better."],[307.78,"And so St."],[308.66,"Peter is trying to turn that around for them."],[311.7,"Say, no, look, remember who Christ is"],[311.9,"Right? So if you following Christ is causing all these things to happen."],[321.18,"And you know that the world out there and the people who are doing this to you are wicked people."],[326.88,"They're not doing this because they're these good and benevolent people."],[329.86,"That's not why they're persecuting you."],[332.03,"Then that means you're like Christ."],[335.71,"That means when we told you, when we baptized you, that you had received the Holy Spirit, that it's true."],[342.85,"That you're now like Christ."],[344.05,"You're now on the same path Christ was on."],[346.93,"That's the sign that you are on the right track, is that all these things are going wrong?"],[353.43,"So these things are. going wrong"],[356.03,"And this is this is important for us on a very practical level."],[366.43,"Because I have found it as someone who hears confession to be a hundred percent true that any time anyone in their life decides to get more serious about their Christian faith."],[383.23,"You know, I'm gonna really, I'm gonna start praying more, I'm gonna do this, I'm gonna do this, I'm gonna do this."],[388.91,"All of a sudden, everything starts going wrong."],[394.32,"Up to it, including, fair warning, everybody I know who's been baptized or charismated and coming to the church, for about a month afterwards, everything goes wrong."],[404.28,"Every Lent, when someone tries to take Lent seriously, all kinds of stuff starts going wrong."],[408.92,"The car doesn't start in the morning."],[410.78,"All of these things start happening."],[413.14,"And this is because, the devil doesn't care when you're not on the right track."],[422.69,"If you're wandering astray, if you're wandering out in the middle of nowhere, not worried about Christ, not worried about the church, not worried about trying to live a Christian life, the last thing the devil wants is for anything to upset you."],[438.53,"Because if something upset you that, might get you to start thinking about things."],[440.69,"And that might get you steered back"],[447.45,"But as soon as we try to make an effort, now he's got something to throw stumbling blocks in our path."],[456.97,"It's all too easy for us to come to that same kind of conclusion."],[462.17,"Forget it. This is too hard."],[465.87,"This is a pain."],[470.48,"And so we need to remember this."],[472.97,"That obstacles and difficulties in life very often."],[478.43,"Very often, are because we are trying to do something worthwhile."],[482.79,"That we are on the right track."],[483.35,"Remember what Christ says"],[486.35,"And that's why it's difficult."],[490.19,"Broad is the way, and easy is the path that leads to destruction."],[495.21,"That's the easy road."],[496.25,"That's the easy way."],[500.17,"So if your approach for the name of Christ, blessed are you, for the spirit of glory and of God rests upon you."],[506.09,"On their part, he is blasphemed."],[508.89,"But on your part, he is glorified."],[513.53,"So when they attack you for following Christ."],[517.75,"So Peter's saying they're blaspheming against the Holy Spirit."],[522.47,"They're not really attacking you."],[525.59,"They're not really criticizing you if they're criticizing you for following Christ."],[530.91,"They're attacking God because they're attacking what the Holy Spirit is doing in your life."],[537.28,"So that's not really an issue between you and them."],[539.84,"That's an issue between them and God."],[543.44,"He says, so that's on their part, but on your part, the Holy Spirit is being glorified when you don't give in."],[550.41,"To what is evil."],[554.33,"Verse 15, but let none of you suffer as a murderer, a thief, an evildoer, or as a busybody in other people's matters."],[561.61,"I love that translation."],[564.73,"This is one of those lists that doesn't seem common sense to us."],[567.89,"Like murderers, thieves, and evildoers, and then like busybody gossips."],[574.35,"We could probably check, or we'd at least like to check ourselves off of those first three."],[578.75,"The fourth one uh catches a lot more of us."],[581.49,"I've never actually killed a guy."],[583.65,"Uh I don't make it a regular habit of stealing things."],[586.61,"But uh I like to think I'm not an evildoer, but uh I have been known to uh swap stories about people when they're not around from time to time."],[596.98,"Um but what's the point here?"],[600.42,"The point isn't that St."],[601.46,"Peter's saying, these are the four things you shouldn't do."],[604.64,"Especially because evildoer covers a lot of ground."],[607.17,"But the point is you don't suffer, you're not suffering for those things."],[612.39,"Remember the thief on the cross next to Christ."],[612.71,"the Who says to other thief, hey, we deserve to be here."],[620.1,"We're criminals. It makes sense that we're being executed, but Christ, this man, Jesus, hasn't done anything."],[628.81,"So again, St."],[630.17,"Peter's reiterating if we're sh-, we're only sharing in Christ's suffering if we're suffering the way Christ did, meaning innocently."],[638.57,"But we get bad consequences for the sins we commit."],[641.77,"That's not suffering for Christ's sake."],[644.09,"That's we bring that upon ourselves."],[646.51,"So he says, so don't let that happen to you."],[648.27,"How do you not let that happen to you?"],[650.45,"Don't do those things."],[652.39,"Don't do those things."],[655.95,"Verse 16, yet if anyone suffers as a Christian, let him not be ashamed, but let him glorify God in this matter."],[664.83,"For the time has come for judgment to begin at the house of God."],[669.39,"And if it begins with us first, what will be the end of those who do not obey the gospel of God?"],[678.35,"Now, if the righteous one is scarcely saved, where will the ungodly and the sinner appear?"],[684.51,"That's from uh Proverbs."],[690.27,"I mentioned the last time St."],[692.03,"Peter is one of the only New Testament writers who quotes Proverbs a lot."],[696.51,"Which is an interesting thing."],[698.79,"Therefore, let those who suffer according to the will of God commit their souls to him in doing good as to a faithful creator."],[706.87,"So he says, he reminds them that, and this is not something new."],[713.03,"He's telling them."],[713.93,"This is all through the Old Testament prophets."],[719.45,"That when the day of the Lord comes."],[721.22,"The day of Yahweh in the Old Testament, day of the Lord of the New Testament, and the day of Christ's glorious appearing."],[727.56,"When that day comes, the judgment starts with the people of God."],[733.58,"So it's not, oh, I'm a Christian."],[735.74,"Oh, I'm in the I'm in the group."],[737.34,"So now I'm immune to judgment."],[739.34,"I'm not going to have to give an account for my actions and and what I've done in this life it's like no no no no no you're up first right St."],[747.46,"Peter's saying right you're up first and so you need to be prepared to give a good account he's saying and imagine if you're up first as a Christian imagine those people who are persecuting you right they're gonna be in a lot of in a lot of trouble if they've been persecuting you for righteousness' sake, rather than than your own sin coming out."],[776.69,"And so if you're suffering according to the will of God, and what that means is not like some people God wants to suffer."],[783.89,"That's not what that means."],[785.53,"' That youre suffering because you're doing what is right, because you're following Christ."],[785.89,"Suffering according to the will of God in this case means for doing the will of God."],[794.19,"When that happens to you, you need to commit your soul to him."],[799.05,"Remember, Christ committed his spirit to God before he died."],[804.17,"But he's saying you do that by doing good, in this life, even while you're suffering."],[814.63,"Even while you're suffering, you do good."],[817.27,"And in that way, you commit, you commit your soul, your life to God, who is the one who created you in the first place."],[825.84,"And who will be faithful to you."],[829.78,"Going forward. So chapter 5, verse 1."],[838.1,"The elders who are among you I exhort, I who am a fellow elder, and a witness of the sufferings of Christ, and also a partaker of the glory that will be revealed."],[849.3,"This is presbyters."],[851.72,"The word that we translate is priests."],[854.04,"But this is also, remember, the presbyters in the Christian community are a continuation of the elders of the people, the presbyters in the old covenant."],[864.14,"Each tribe, each clan had elders, had presbyters."],[868.2,"And so, in the same way, we saw in uh 1 andst 2 Timothy and Titus, and we saw in the book of Acts that Saint Paul and the other apostles appointed press or set elders over every Christian community."],[882.56,"They followed the same pattern from the old the old testament."],[885.85,"And so now Saint Peter is saying, Let me address the presbyters there."],[891.55,"The people in each of these communities who are sort of the elders and who are in charge."],[896.8,"And he says, He's a fellow press room, he he has this role, in the in the Christian community, and he is a witness of the sufferings of Christ."],[906.18,"This is St."],[906.74,"Peter, he's an apostle, he was there, and also a partaker of the glory that will be revealed."],[912.42,"What did he just say a few verses ago?"],[915.14,"ade M you a partaker of the glory to be revealed."],[919.74,"That you suffered, you shared in Christ's sufferings."],[922.8,"So this is Saint Peter saying, Here's why I can speak to you."],[926.48,"I know you're the elders."],[928.41,"And you're the ones in charge, but here's why I'm going, I am I speak to you, because I also am a Presbyter."],[935.61,"I'm an eyewitness of Christ."],[937.63,"And knew him, and I've also suffered as he suffered."],[942.77,"And so that is what gives me the authority now to speak to you."],[948.69,"Verse 2 Shepherd the flock of God which is among you, serving as overseers, not by compulsion but willingly, not for dishonest gain, but eagerly, nor as being lords over those entrusted to you, but being examples to the flock."],[967.05,"So he uses this extended metaphor of shepherds."],[972.51,"This is, of course, is used throughout the Old Testament to refer to the leadership of Israel as a whole."],[982.11,"So both the presbyters, the elders of the tribes, but also the king, the high priest, anyone in authority."],[988.69,"You'll see the shepherds of Israel."],[991.01,"You know, he hararkenkano, shepherds of Israel, and then there's usually a bunch of judgment coming."],[995.74,"For the prophet, because they haven't been doing their jobs properly."],[998.6,"But so St."],[999.72,"Peter, notice, picks this up and applies it directly to now in the Christian community."],[1002.6,"now The leadership, who are the shepherds."],[1009.2,"And so he says you need to shepherd them, serving as overseers."],[1012.72,"That's the word episcope."],[1015.46,"That we translate as as bishop."],[1018.5,"Um or transliterate, kind of."],[1021.7,"But anyway, um, as bishop."],[1024.42,"Um, but that also were that word, remember, comes from the Greek translation in the Old Testament of a Hebrew word that referred to like a herdsman."],[1036.26,"So this is part of that shepherd metaphor, too."],[1039.3,"That's why it gets translated pastor, which means shepherd in uh Latin."],[1045.42,"So this is extending that."],[1045.46,"So he's refocusing how they think about this."],[1052.57,"Because at least at this point in history, um the uh the emperor did not think of himself as a shepherd."],[1062.41,"We'll put it that way."],[1063.95,"The title imperator means conqueror."],[1067.28,"Um, and he thought of himself as a god mostly."],[1070.72,"Um, but um a shepherd notice is not the person who owns the sheep."],[1081.7,"A shepherd or a herdsman is the person who's entrusted with the sheep, which are precious to the person who owns them."],[1091.9,"And he was entrusted to care for them."],[1095.1,"And is going to have to give an account for the kind of job he does."],[1099.1,"That's an important part of this reframing."],[1101.83,"And that's why that metaphor becomes so common in the Old Testament is God is trying to remind them hey, you don't own these people."],[1111.83,"They aren't yours to do with as you please."],[1115.64,"They belong to their God's people."],[1119.16,"And he just put you in charge to take care of them."],[1122.42,"And make sure to make sure they stay healthy and safe."],[1126.6,"And so he says, not by compulsion, but willingly."],[1132.05,"Meaning that is now it was possible for someone to look at this sort of job as a chore."],[1139.37,"Oh, I guess."],[1140.41,"Another pro you know, another issue."],[1142.55,"Um, but that they need to be willing, and he's about to say eager, even, to help care for the people of God who have been entrusted for them."],[1155.01,"Uh, not for dishonest gain."],[1157.65,"That's not new either."],[1160.15,"Already then there were people who sought positions of authority so that they could use them for dishonest gain."],[1165.75,"I mean, Judas did that."],[1167.57,"One of the 12 disciples did that."],[1169.89,"Um, so that's not new either, but is wrong."],[1172.45,"Nor is being lords over those entrusted to you"],[1177.4,"But being examples to the flock."],[1180.58,"So the contrast here is between lord and example."],[1184.34,"And this is forms an important part of our theology of church leadership."],[1190.12,"Is that uh you are not the boss."],[1194.14,"The bishop is not the lord of the church in the Orthodox Church."],[1198.95,"He is not a prince."],[1201.4,"He is not a king, he is not, you know, a slave master."],[1206.9,"He is to be an example."],[1208.76,"Specifically, an example of what?"],[1211.0,"An example of Christ."],[1213.18,"So for us, the bishop, for example, is an eye, is to be an icon of Christ to the people."],[1220.59,"He is not their boss."],[1223.25,"He does not lord it over them."],[1225.33,"He does not use compulsion."],[1230.18,"And so St."],[1231.14,"Peter's already. Because of course, humans are sinful and they don't change that much."],[1242.49,"Verse 4, and when the chief shepherd appears, you will receive the crown of glory that does not fade away."],[1250.74,"So Christ, remember, who's the head shepherd."],[1253.62,"The uh the great high priest"],[1256.71,"When he when he appears, the appearance of Christ comes, he's the one who's going to demand an account from the shepherds he put over his flock."],[1266.57,"And if they've done it the right way, willingly, eagerly, serving his examples to the flock, then they'll receive a reward, for having served in this role."],[1281.11,"Otherwise, not so much."],[1284.71,"Otherwise, they're going to be again."],[1286.67,"Remember where the judgment starts."],[1290.84,"Verse 5. Likewise, you younger people, submit yourselves to your elders."],[1296.56,"Yes, all of you be submissive to one another, and be clothed with humility, for God resists the proud, but gives grace to the humble."],[1306.56,"Guess where that's from?"],[1309.28,"Proverbs. So um he says, You younger people, which is really talking about everybody else."],[1320.59,"Who is isn't an elder, you need to submit yourselves to your elders."],[1325.89,"Uh be a sheep, not a goat."],[1328.23,"Sheep sheep generally do what the shepherd tells them."],[1331.59,"Goats generally do not do what anyone tells them."],[1335.84,"And so um why?"],[1339.48,"It's because, as he's just said, they're gonna be held to account."],[1344.77,"And if they're gonna be held to account, if if my bishop who is in charge of me is gonna be held to account by Christ, then that means he's not held to account by me."],[1357.03,"And I don't need to sit here and when he tells me to do something, well, is that really the right thing to do?"],[1363.51,"Is this what I should do?"],[1364.63,"Should I say yes?"],[1365.51,"Should I say no?"],[1367.88,"I don't need to do that."],[1369.88,"Christ, he's accountable to Christ."],[1371.8,"Christ will hold him accountable."],[1374.68,"Uh Saint Siloon said regarding this, that uh he put it pretty bluntly, God doesn't punish. sin twice"],[1385.26,"So he was saying, and this isn't a programmatic statement."],[1389.12,"Just understand the point he's making."],[1390.56,"He's saying, if you know, someone who is in spiritual authority over you told you to do something, and it turned out that was a sin, but you obeyed them, it would be the person who told you to do that who would be considered guilty of that sin, not you."],[1407.77,"If we're disobedient and make all of our own decisions, then we're the ones held to account for all of our decisions."],[1413.47,"But he's saying if you voluntarily, because remember, they're not lording it over you."],[1419.05,"If you voluntarily submit to someone as being a spiritual authority over you, and you're obedient to them, then it's they who have to answer for their relationship with you."],[1432.26,"That's the dynamic that St."],[1434.98,"Peter is talking about here."],[1439.22,"And then notice he follows that up with all of you be submissive to one another."],[1445.99,"And now you say, well, how does that work?"],[1448.23,"I mean, if everybody's submissive, nobody would ever do anything."],[1450.47,"That's not what he's talking about."],[1451.84,"He's talking about the opposite of what tends to happen, which is each of us has an opinion, at least one."],[1461.2,"Sometimes you get 12 people together, you have 15 opinions, but each of us has at least one opinion."],[1466.4,"We all think our opinion is right."],[1468.6,"And so when we get together to discuss something, we tend to argue that no, my the specific details of my opinion and my way of seeing things is right."],[1478.52,"And we all argue with each other."],[1481.02,"So what's the opposite of that?"],[1483.5,"The opposite of that is being humble enough to say, well, hey, maybe my opinion at least does not contain the whole truth."],[1491.4,"Maybe my way of seeing things is valid, but there are other perspectives that I could learn."],[1496.98,"And if everyone comes to a discussion within the Christian community with that kind of humility."],[1503.24,"Of like, here's what I have to offer to this conversation, but I don't think I have the entirety of the truth."],[1508.84,"I'm not arrogant enough to think that."],[1511.13,"Then we can have a productive discussion and all learn from each other."],[1514.41,"And the community can function together."],[1517.55,"Whereas if we're all proud and arrogant and think we know everything and we all show up to fight it out, we're not gonna get anything done."],[1526.67,"And so he then quotes Proverbs."],[1528.93,"God resists the proud."],[1530.21,"Why? Why does God resist the proud?"],[1534.53,"Because he just hates proud people."],[1537.49,"No, it's to humble them."],[1542.42,"But he gives grace to the humble."],[1545.24,"Meaning, if you're proud, God's gonna take you down a peg or two."],[1549.56,"If you're humble, God's gonna lift you up."],[1552.04,"Many who are last will be first, and many who are first will be last, as Christ said over and over and over again"],[1562.05,"Verse 6. Therefore, humble yourselves under the mighty hand of God that he may exalt you in due time."],[1569.97,"Casting all your care upon him, for he cares for you."],[1578.61,"So he summarizes that."],[1579.73,"Humble yourselves under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time."],[1583.23,"You humble yourself, he'll lift you up."],[1586.41,"So, what would be an obstacle to us humbling ourselves?"],[1590.33,"What is it that sort of motivates that pride and makes us want to push for our opinion and our way of doing things?"],[1598.97,"Because there are things we're concerned about, where there are things we're worried about happening."],[1604.79,"I think bad thing X is gonna happen."],[1607.51,"I have to stop it from happening."],[1608.95,"So I have to convince all these people that I'm right or the whole church is gonna fall apart and everything's gonna go bad."],[1616.04,"We're worried about these things."],[1618.44,"That creates this sense of anxiety and urgency in us that no, I have to show them, that I'm right."],[1626.74,"Whereas if we give our cares to God to take care of."],[1631.72,"If I accept that, no, what happens to this parish or the church as a whole, or this community, what's going to happen to them in the future is in the hands of God, not mine."],[1645.4,"Not mine. If I let go of that pride thinking, uh no, I am the one who will do this, then I don't have to."],[1654.13,"It takes it away from me."],[1657.35,"When I was a kid, Smokey the Bear kept telling me that only I could prevent forest fires."],[1662.17,"And obviously that's not true."],[1666.22,"And so when we understand that, we can let go."],[1669.34,"And that allows us to approach things with humility."],[1673.66,"Because me figuring it out and forcing everybody to go along with it is not what's crucial."],[1681.14,"Verse, be sober, be vigilant, because your adversary, the devil, walks about like a roaring lion, seeking whom he may devour."],[1691.78,"Okay. So, who's the real enemy?"],[1696.34,"You notice he's gone through all this, these people persecuting them."],[1699.86,"They're humans doing all this bad stuff to them."],[1702.9,"He never really calls them the enemy."],[1705.14,"He never tells them to resist them, he says the opposite."],[1708.52,"Don't resist them, don't fight back, don't take revenge."],[1712.69,"Why? Because this is the real enemy."],[1716.95,"The real enemy is the devil prowling around."],[1719.11,"And if I go and I start hating someone because of how they've treated me."],[1723.27,"Then that gives the real enemy an opening"],[1728.39,"To get at me."],[1731.19,"If someone hates me and I love them in return, devil's not going to get me."],[1739.24,"Because then I'm with Christ."],[1740.52,"So this is the flip side."],[1741.72,"That's the real enemy."],[1742.84,"That's what we should really be worried about."],[1744.76,"Not the persecution that humans can do to us."],[1748.8,"But him. And so we need to we need to be sober and vigilant."],[1752.16,"Verse 9, resist him steadfast in the faith, knowing that the same sufferings are experienced by your brotherhood in all the world."],[1762.24,"So the things we suffer are not unique to us."],[1767.08,"In fact, if we're talking to people living in the United States today, at least right now, any sufferings we face for being Christians are pretty low grade compared to what Christians are suffering in other parts of the world right now and have in history."],[1781.96,"That may change."],[1784.36,"Somebody could have said the same in Russia in 1910."],[1788.04,"But could change."],[1790.12,"But right now at least."],[1806.76,"Verse 10, but may the God of all grace who called us to his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after you have suffered a while, perfect, establish, strengthen, and settle you."],[1820.08,"Notice that last word, settle."],[1823.22,"Keep in mind what these communities have just experienced."],[1828.39,"So he's saying the suffering will go on for a while."],[1832.55,"There will be a time of suffering."],[1835.45,"But after that, if you remain faithful through that suffering to Christ and following him, then after that, remember, perfect is mature."],[1845.15,"Complete. The suffering is going to bring you to maturity."],[1849.24,"It's going to establish you."],[1850.52,"You're going to become stronger, and ultimately, God's going to settle you."],[1852.68,"In a place"],[1856.94,"To him be the glory and the dominion forever and ever."],[1860.46,"Amen. Verse 12 by Sylvanus, our faithful brother, as I consider him, I have written to you briefly, exhorting him and testifying that this is the true grace of God in which you stand."],[1875.02,"Okay, so Saint Sylvanus is the one who's bringing this letter to them."],[1881.9,"Excuse me. It's the one who's carrying the letter."],[1887.74,"Probably not. Um he could be."],[1892.38,"There's like five journal articles debatinging the exact word of this."],[1896.62,"the exact. So from Greek wording of this, he's definitely the one who carried the letter"],[1904.42,"It actually doesn't say whether he's the one who wrote it or not."],[1908.58,"So maybe. But he's definitely the one who carried it to them and read it to them in those communities."],[1917.62,"Um so he's kind of by putting that on there, he's saying, Yes, I know it's not me."],[1926.52,"This is the person who I sent with it."],[1928.28,"So listen to what he says."],[1929.4,"Because remember, the person who brought the letter wouldn't just read it once and then move on."],[1934.06,"He'd read it and then he was supposed to be prepared to answer questions."],[1938.16,"And interact and everything."],[1939.84,"So St. Peter is basically saying, This is this is Saint Sylvanus, St."],[1945.0,"Silwan, it's the same name."],[1946.76,"Um, this is this is the one who I'm sending."],[1950.48,"With the letter to answer your questions."],[1954.13,"Do these things."],[1956.45,"Verse 13, she who is in Babylon, elect together with you, greets you, and so does Mark my son."],[1964.85,"Uh there wasn't a Babylon at this time of history, really."],[1969.73,"Yes. So this is this is code."],[1972.77,"Why would Saint Peter, if he's still in Rome, use code?"],[1977.49,"Because he's a Jew and they all just got thrown out of Rome."],[1980.43,"He's Jewish. They always got thrown out of Rome."],[1983.39,"So he's saying he's not too far out from his martyrdom"],[1989.55,"Next emperor is the one who's going to kill him."],[1993.07,"But so this is code."],[1996.29,"The role that Babylon played in the Old Testament, as sort of the city that was sort of the embodiment of sort of evil in the world, like the Tower of Babel on."],[2007.95,"Is now Rome."],[2011.53,"In the first century AD."],[2013.31,"And so that's kind of code."],[2014.63,"And that she who is elect with you is talking about the church."],[2018.44,"So he's saying the community, the Christian community, the church in Rome, Babylon."],[2024.22,"Greets you. Um Mark, that's Saint Mark who wrote the gospel."],[2033.2,"Remember, the gospel is written around AD 69 by Saint Mark after St."],[2038.64,"Peter's martyrdom. He went to Egypt and wrote down Saint Peter's preaching about Christ, his testimony about Christ."],[2046.56,"Verse 14 greet one another with a kiss of love."],[2049.6,"Peace to you all who are in Christ Jesus."],[2052.32,"Amen. So that is uh the end of 1 Peter."],[2060.4,"So we'll probably conclude for tonight, even though that's a little short."],[2066.56,"And uh next time, even though it's out of order, as I said, we're gonna do uh the Epistle of St."],[2074.2,"Jude next. And the reason we're doing it next is that as we talked about in the big long introduction, that ends up get the the epistle of Saint Jude ends up getting incorporated into 2 Peter."],[2089.16,"So we're gonna read Saint Jude's epistle first because of that."],[2093.4,"And that way, then when we're going through 2 Peter, we'll be able to see where it's worked in and how that works, and talk about that more when we're in Second Peter."],[2103.72,"So thank you, everybody."],[2107.16,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2114.36,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2119.84,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":0.16,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: two approaches in 1 Peter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Over last couple chapters Peter takes <b>two approaches</b></li><li class=\"d0\">First: remind them of <b>Christ's sufferings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">killed by <b>sinful men</b>, then entered into his <b>glory</b></li><li class=\"d1\">share his sufferings → share his <b>glory</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Remind them of <b>Christ's second coming</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Other side: within the Christian community, <b>love and mutual support</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>united</b>, there for each other, <b>doing good</b> to each other</li><li class=\"d1\">against what's coming from the outside world</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Solidarity</b> as they prepare for the second coming</li><li class=\"d0\">Make sure suffering is <b>unjust</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't get persecuted for doing <b>actual bad things</b> - then it's not persecution</li><li class=\"d1\">persecuted for doing good → <b>like Christ</b>, suffering for what is right</li><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>1 Peter 4:12</b></li></ul>"},{"t":104.29,"lv":2,"h":"1 Peter 4:12-13 - Don't think it's strange","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Fiery trial</b> - \"do not think it strange\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Rejoice</b> to the extent you partake of <b>Christ's sufferings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">when his glory is revealed, <b>glad with exceeding joy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Summarizing the last chapter or two</li><li class=\"d0\">Don't act like it's some <b>strange thing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Why is this happening?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Just remember: Christ was <b>sinless</b>, yet suffered at the hands of <b>wicked people</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Happens to you too → <b>you're like Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">When he <b>appears again</b> → you share his glory, with <b>joy</b></li></ul>"},{"t":164.63,"lv":3,"h":"4:14 - Reproached for Christ's name","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Blessed are you, for the Spirit of glory and of God rests upon you\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Now he's talking about the <b>Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Persecuted, mocked, <b>marginalized</b>, <b>shunned</b> for following Christ</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sign the Holy Spirit is within you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Goes against how the ancient world - and <b>we</b> - normally operate</li><li class=\"d0\">Our pattern: make a major decision (join a club, get a degree)</li><li class=\"d1\">everything starts going wrong → \"<b>maybe I shouldn't be doing this</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"all the signs are this is the wrong thing\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Natural in the ancient world too</li></ul>"},{"t":230.76,"lv":3,"h":"The temptation Peter is answering","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Members of the <b>Jewish community in the synagogue</b></li><li class=\"d1\">apostles (<b>Peter, Paul</b>) came preaching <b>Jesus of Nazareth is the Messiah</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"this gospel thing, we're on board\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Join the Christian part → <b>forced out of their homes in Rome</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>shunned</b> by society, \"everything falling apart\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Even <b>within</b> the Christian community</li><li class=\"d1\">Peter telling them to love one another → <b>they're not all doing that</b></li><li class=\"d1\">people they don't get along with, problems, difficulties</li><li class=\"d0\">Easy to say \"<b>why am I doing this again?</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if this is true, why did everything go bad as soon as I joined?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"maybe I need to go back to where I was, when things were better\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter turns it around: <b>remember who Christ is</b></li><li class=\"d1\">following Christ causes this; persecutors are <b>wicked</b>, not \"good and benevolent\"</li><li class=\"d1\">→ you're <b>like Christ</b>; the <b>Holy Spirit</b> you received at baptism is real</li><li class=\"d1\">on the same path Christ was on: <b>things going wrong = sign you're on the right track</b></li></ul>"},{"t":366.43,"lv":3,"h":"Practical: confession and \"everything goes wrong\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Important on a <b>very practical level</b></li><li class=\"d0\">As one who <b>hears confession</b>: \"a hundred percent true\"</li><li class=\"d1\">anyone who gets more <b>serious about the faith</b> (prays more, etc.) → everything starts going wrong</li><li class=\"d0\">Fair warning: after <b>baptism or chrismation</b>, about <b>a month</b> where everything goes wrong</li><li class=\"d0\">Every <b>Lent</b>, someone takes it seriously → \"the car doesn't start in the morning\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why: the <b>devil doesn't care</b> when you're not on the right track</li><li class=\"d1\">wandering astray, not worried about Christ or church → <b>last thing he wants is to upset you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">upset might get you thinking → <b>steered back</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Make an effort → now he has <b>stumbling blocks</b> to throw</li><li class=\"d0\">Easy to conclude \"<b>forget it, too hard, a pain</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Remember: obstacles very often = <b>trying to do something worthwhile</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Christ: \"<b>broad is the way and easy is the path that leads to destruction</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":500.17,"lv":3,"h":"Blasphemed vs. glorified","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>On their part he is blasphemed, but on your part he is glorified</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Attack you for following Christ → really <b>blaspheming the Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not really criticizing you</li><li class=\"d1\">attacking <b>what the Holy Spirit is doing in your life</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not an issue between you and them → <b>between them and God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">On your part: Spirit <b>glorified</b> when you <b>don't give in to what is evil</b></li></ul>"},{"t":554.33,"lv":2,"h":"4:15 - Murderer, thief, busybody","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Let none of you suffer as a <b>murderer, thief, evildoer</b>, or <b>busybody in other people's matters</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"I love that translation\"</li><li class=\"d0\">List that doesn't seem common sense</li><li class=\"d1\">we can check ourselves off the <b>first three</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>fourth catches a lot more of us</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I have been known to <b>swap stories about people</b> when they're not around\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Point is <b>not</b> \"these are the four things you shouldn't do\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>evildoer</b> covers a lot of ground</li><li class=\"d0\">Point: you're <b>not suffering for those things</b></li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>thief on the cross</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>we deserve to be here</b>... but this man hasn't done anything\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Share Christ's suffering only if suffering <b>innocently</b></li><li class=\"d1\">bad consequences for our sins = \"we bring that upon ourselves\"</li><li class=\"d0\">How not to? <b>Don't do those things</b></li></ul>"},{"t":655.95,"lv":2,"h":"4:16-19 - Judgment begins at the house of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"If anyone suffers as a <b>Christian</b>, let him <b>not be ashamed</b>, but <b>glorify God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Judgment to begin at the house of God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">if it begins with us, \"what will be the end of those who do not obey the gospel?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"If the righteous one is <b>scarcely saved</b>...\" - from <b>Proverbs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Peter one of the only NT writers who <b>quotes Proverbs a lot</b> - interesting</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Commit their souls</b> to him in doing good as to a <b>faithful creator</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not new - all through the <b>OT prophets</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>day of Yahweh</b> / day of the Lord / Christ's glorious appearing → judgment starts with <b>God's people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I'm in the group, so <b>immune</b>\" - not exempt from giving an account</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>You're up first</b>\" → be prepared to give a good account</li><li class=\"d0\">Imagine <b>persecutors</b> if believers are up first</li><li class=\"d1\">persecuted for <b>righteousness' sake</b>, not own sin → \"a lot of trouble\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>According to the will of God</b>\" ≠ God wants some to suffer</li><li class=\"d1\">= suffering <b>for doing the will of God</b>, following Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Commit your soul: Christ <b>committed his spirit</b> to God before he died</li><li class=\"d1\">how: <b>do good, even while suffering</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to the God who <b>created</b> you and <b>will be faithful</b> going forward</li></ul>"},{"t":829.78,"lv":2,"h":"1 Peter 5:1 - Peter's word to the elders","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"The <b>elders</b> among you I exhort, I who am a <b>fellow elder</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">= <b>presbyters</b> - the word we translate <b>\"priests\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Continuation of the <b>elders of the people</b> in the old covenant</li><li class=\"d1\">each tribe, each clan had <b>presbyters</b></li><li class=\"d1\">1-2 <b>Timothy, Titus, Acts</b>: Paul and apostles <b>set elders over every community</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same pattern from the OT</li><li class=\"d0\">Addressing those <b>in charge</b> of each community</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter: <b>witness of the sufferings of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">apostle, \"he was there\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"Partaker of the glory that will be revealed\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">echoes what he said a few verses ago: you share in the sufferings</li><li class=\"d0\">Why he can speak: <b>fellow presbyter, eyewitness</b> who knew Christ, <b>suffered as he suffered</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"that is what gives me the <b>authority</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":948.69,"lv":2,"h":"5:2-3 - Shepherd the flock","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Shepherd the flock of God</b> among you, serving as overseers, <b>not by compulsion but willingly</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not for <b>dishonest gain</b>, but eagerly; nor <b>lords</b> over those entrusted, but <b>examples</b> to the flock\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Extended shepherd metaphor</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Used throughout the OT for <b>leadership of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">elders of the tribes, but also <b>king, high priest</b>, anyone in authority</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Hearken, <b>O shepherds of Israel</b>\" → usually a bunch of judgment: <b>not doing their jobs</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Peter applies it directly to <b>Christian leadership</b> - now the shepherds</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Serving as overseers\" = <i>episkope</i></li><li class=\"d1\">we <b>transliterate</b> it as <b>bishop</b></li><li class=\"d1\">comes from the Greek OT translation of a Hebrew word for a <b>herdsman</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Part of the shepherd metaphor → \"<b>pastor</b>\" = shepherd in Latin</li></ul>"},{"t":1045.46,"lv":3,"h":"Reframing: the shepherd doesn't own the sheep","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Refocusing</b> how they think about leadership</li><li class=\"d0\">At this point the <b>emperor</b> didn't think of himself as a shepherd</li><li class=\"d1\">title <i>imperator</i> = <b>conqueror</b></li><li class=\"d1\">thought of himself \"as a <b>god</b> mostly\"</li><li class=\"d0\">A shepherd is <b>not the owner</b> of the sheep</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>entrusted</b> with sheep precious to the owner</li><li class=\"d1\">must <b>give an account</b> for the job he does</li><li class=\"d0\">Why the metaphor is so common in the OT</li><li class=\"d1\">God reminding them: \"<b>you don't own these people</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not yours to do with as you please\" - <b>God's people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">you're put in charge to keep them <b>healthy and safe</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1126.6,"lv":3,"h":"Willingly, not for gain, not lording it","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Not by compulsion but willingly</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">possible to see the job as a <b>chore</b> - \"another issue\"</li><li class=\"d1\">must be willing - even <b>eager</b> - to care for God's people</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Not for dishonest gain</b>\" - not new</li><li class=\"d1\">already people sought authority for <b>dishonest gain</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Judas</b> did - one of the twelve</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Nor being <b>lords</b>... but <b>examples</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">contrast: <b>lord vs. example</b></li><li class=\"d1\">important part of our <b>theology of church leadership</b></li><li class=\"d0\">The bishop is <b>not the lord</b> of the church in the Orthodox Church</li><li class=\"d1\">not a <b>prince</b>, king, or <b>slave master</b></li><li class=\"d1\">an <b>example of Christ</b> - \"an <b>icon of Christ</b> to the people\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not their boss; no lording it, no compulsion</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter already addressing this - \"humans are sinful and <b>they don't change that much</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1242.49,"lv":3,"h":"5:4 - The chief shepherd appears","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"When the <b>chief shepherd</b> appears, you will receive the <b>crown of glory that does not fade away</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Christ</b> = head shepherd, the <b>great high priest</b></li><li class=\"d0\">When he appears he <b>demands an account</b> from the shepherds he put over his flock</li><li class=\"d0\">Done it the right way</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>willingly, eagerly</b>, as examples → <b>reward</b> for serving in this role</li><li class=\"d0\">Otherwise: \"<b>not so much</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">remember where <b>judgment starts</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1290.84,"lv":2,"h":"5:5 - Younger, submit to elders","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Likewise, <b>you younger people, submit yourselves to your elders</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"all of you be <b>submissive to one another</b>, and be <b>clothed with humility</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"God <b>resists the proud</b>, but gives <b>grace to the humble</b>\" - from <b>Proverbs</b> again</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Younger\" really = <b>everybody who isn't an elder</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Be a sheep, not a goat</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">sheep generally do what the shepherd tells them</li><li class=\"d1\">goats \"generally do not do what anyone tells them\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why: the shepherds will be <b>held to account</b></li><li class=\"d1\">my bishop is accountable to <b>Christ</b>, not to me</li><li class=\"d1\">I don't need to second-guess: \"is that really the right thing to do? should I say yes? no?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ will hold him accountable</li></ul>"},{"t":1374.68,"lv":3,"h":"St. Silouan: God doesn't punish sin twice","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Silouan</b>, \"pretty bluntly\": \"<b>God doesn't punish sin twice</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not a programmatic statement\" - understand the <b>point</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Someone in <b>spiritual authority</b> tells you to do something, it turns out a <b>sin</b>, but you obeyed</li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>one who told you</b> is guilty, <b>not you</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Disobedient, making <b>all your own decisions</b> → you're held to account for all of them</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Voluntarily</b> submit to someone as spiritual authority and obey</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they're not lording it over you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>they</b> answer for their relationship with you</li><li class=\"d0\">That's the dynamic Peter is talking about</li></ul>"},{"t":1439.22,"lv":3,"h":"\"All of you be submissive to one another\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Well, how does that work? <b>If everybody's submissive, nobody would ever do anything</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not what he's talking about</li><li class=\"d0\">The <b>opposite of what tends to happen</b></li><li class=\"d1\">each of us has <b>at least one opinion</b>; \"12 people, <b>15 opinions</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">all think ours is right → we <b>argue</b> with each other</li><li class=\"d0\">Opposite = <b>humble enough</b> to say \"my opinion <b>doesn't contain the whole truth</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">my view may be valid, but <b>other perspectives</b> I could learn</li><li class=\"d0\">Come to discussion with humility: \"here's what I have to offer... <b>not arrogant enough</b> to think I have the entirety\"</li><li class=\"d1\">→ <b>productive discussion</b>, all learn, community functions</li><li class=\"d0\">All proud, show up \"to <b>fight it out</b>\" → <b>nothing gets done</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Quotes <b>Proverbs</b>: \"God resists the proud\"</li><li class=\"d1\">why? not because \"he just hates proud people\"</li><li class=\"d1\">proud: God takes you <b>down a peg or two</b>; humble: he <b>lifts you up</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>many who are last will be first</b>, and many who are first last\" - Christ \"over and over\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1562.05,"lv":2,"h":"5:6-7 - Humble yourselves, cast your cares","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Humble yourselves under the mighty hand of God</b>, that he may <b>exalt you in due time</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Casting all your care upon him</b>, for he cares for you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Humble yourself → <b>he'll lift you up</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Obstacle to humility</b>: what motivates pride, pushing for my way?</li><li class=\"d1\">things we're <b>worried about</b>: \"bad thing X is going to happen, I have to stop it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">must convince everyone or \"the whole church is going to fall apart\"</li><li class=\"d1\">creates <b>anxiety and urgency</b>: \"I have to show them I'm right\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Instead <b>give our cares to God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">future of the parish / the church / the community is <b>in the hands of God, not mine</b></li><li class=\"d1\">let go of the pride \"I am the one who will do this\" → \"<b>then I don't have to</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Smokey the Bear</b>: \"only I could prevent forest fires\" - obviously not true</li><li class=\"d0\">Understand that → <b>let go</b>, approach with <b>humility</b></li><li class=\"d1\">me figuring it out and <b>forcing everybody to go along</b> is not crucial</li></ul>"},{"t":1681.14,"lv":2,"h":"5:8 - The real enemy","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Be <b>sober, be vigilant</b>, because your adversary the <b>devil</b> walks about like a <b>roaring lion</b>, seeking whom he may devour\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Who's the <b>real enemy</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">humans persecuting them - Peter <b>never calls them the enemy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">never tells them to resist them; the <b>opposite</b>: don't resist, don't fight back, <b>no revenge</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why: the <b>devil</b> is the real enemy</li><li class=\"d1\">start <b>hating</b> someone for how they treated me → <b>opening</b> for the real enemy</li><li class=\"d1\">they hate me, I <b>love them in return</b> → \"devil's not going to get me\" - <b>I'm with Christ</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Flip side: what we should really worry about is <b>him</b>, not human persecution</li><li class=\"d0\">So be <b>sober and vigilant</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1752.16,"lv":3,"h":"5:9-11 - Same sufferings; God will settle you","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Resist him, steadfast in the faith</b>, knowing the same sufferings are experienced by your <b>brotherhood in all the world</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Our sufferings <b>not unique</b></li><li class=\"d1\">in the US today, sufferings for being Christian are \"<b>pretty low grade</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">compared to Christians elsewhere now and in history</li><li class=\"d1\">\"that may change\" - but right now</li><li class=\"d0\">Nothing you're going through that your <b>brothers and sisters worldwide</b> aren't experiencing</li><li class=\"d0\">5:10: \"God of all grace who called us to his <b>eternal glory</b>... after you have suffered a while, <b>perfect, establish, strengthen, settle you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">note last word: <b>settle</b> - keep in mind what these communities just experienced</li><li class=\"d1\">suffering goes on for <b>a while</b></li><li class=\"d1\">remain faithful → <i>perfect</i> = <b>mature, complete</b></li><li class=\"d1\">suffering brings you to <b>maturity</b>, <b>establishes</b>, makes you <b>stronger</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ultimately God <b>settles you in a place</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"To him be the glory and the dominion forever and ever. <b>Amen</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1860.46,"lv":2,"h":"5:12 - Sylvanus, the letter-bearer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"By <b>Sylvanus</b>, our faithful brother... I have written to you briefly, exhorting and testifying this is the <b>true grace of God</b> in which you stand\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Sylvanus = the one <b>carrying the letter</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Did he <b>write</b> it? \"Probably not. He could be.\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"like <b>five journal articles</b> debating the exact wording\"</li><li class=\"d1\">exact Greek: <b>definitely carried it</b>; doesn't say whether he <b>wrote</b> it - \"maybe\"</li><li class=\"d1\">carried it and <b>read it to them</b> in those communities</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter by naming him: \"I know it's not me - this is the person <b>I sent with it</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">The bearer wouldn't read it once and move on</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>prepared to answer questions</b> and interact</li><li class=\"d0\">Sylvanus = <b>St. Silouan</b> - \"same name\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter sending him with the letter to answer your questions</li></ul>"},{"t":1956.45,"lv":3,"h":"5:13-14 - Babylon, Mark, and the kiss of love","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>She who is in Babylon</b>, elect together with you, greets you, and so does <b>Mark, my son</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">No real Babylon at this time → <b>code</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why code if Peter is in <b>Rome</b>? He's <b>Jewish</b>; they all just got <b>thrown out of Rome</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not far from <b>martyrdom</b>; the next emperor is the one who'll kill him</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Babylon's OT role</b>: city that embodied <b>evil in the world</b>, like the <b>Tower of Babel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now = <b>Rome</b> in the first century AD</li><li class=\"d0\">\"She who is elect with you\" = <b>the church</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the Christian community in Rome / \"Babylon\" greets you</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Mark</b> = St. Mark who wrote the <b>gospel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">written ~<b>AD 69</b> after Peter's martyrdom</li><li class=\"d1\">went to <b>Egypt</b>, wrote down Peter's preaching and testimony about Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">5:14: \"Greet one another with a <b>kiss of love</b>. <b>Peace</b> to you all who are in Christ Jesus. Amen.\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2052.32,"lv":2,"h":"End of 1 Peter; what's next","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"That is the <b>end of 1 Peter</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Conclude for tonight, \"even though that's a little short\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Next time, \"even though it's out of order\": <b>Epistle of St. Jude</b></li><li class=\"d1\">reason (from the <b>big long introduction</b>): Jude gets <b>incorporated into 2 Peter</b></li><li class=\"d1\">read Jude first → going through 2 Peter, see <b>where it's worked in</b> and how</li><li class=\"d1\">talk about it more in <b>Second Peter</b></li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: <b>Epistle of St. Jude</b> (out of order) - before <b>2 Peter</b>"});
